(5590205, 808649, 17153, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by fridjo:</b></div><hr/><i> love the colors &amp; sharpness and isolation from the background, although there is some colored banding visible in the background </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>no, sorry, there''s no color banding, just didn''t notice that I had color settings on 16-bit. but still gave you 9, since I suspected the problem might be be on my side :) this one I really liked</td>', 'Originally posted by fridjo: love the colors & sharpness and isolation from the background, although there is some colored banding visible in the background   no, sorry, there''s no color banding, just didn''t notice that I had color settings on 16-bit. but still gave you 9, since I suspected the problem might be be on my side :) this one I really liked', '2009-07-29 10:55:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(5590226, 808489, 30861, '<td valign="top">Geeze, I can''t believe this image got so utterly hammered, holy smokes! I''m the one that gave you your lone 10, and I can''t understand how this image failed to move at least a few more viewers. The sense of stark, surreal immediacy, the inarticulate *foreboding* of the image, are just remarkable. But evidently I''m way out of tune with the rest of the voters on this one, and you know, I don''t care! I''m making you the second-ever winner of the Golden Bear award :-)<br/> <br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=762723" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/30000-34999/30861/120/762723.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/30000-34999/30861/120/762723.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/30000-34999/30861/120/762723.jpg"/></a> <br/> <br/>R.</td>', 'Geeze, I can''t believe this image got so utterly hammered, holy smokes! I''m the one that gave you your lone 10, and I can''t understand how this image failed to move at least a few more viewers. The sense of stark, surreal immediacy, the inarticulate *foreboding* of the image, are just remarkable. But evidently I''m way out of tune with the rest of the voters on this one, and you know, I don''t care! I''m making you the second-ever winner of the Golden Bear award :-)   R.', '2009-07-29 11:03:44.000000', NULL, 0),
