(5592967, 808494, 76335, '<td valign="top">I''ve been out of touch the last week or so. I meant to follow up on your entry, as I didn''t get around to voting. Anyway, I sort of remember hastily suggesting this title -- probably in jest. But really, I love it! A quirky shot needs a quirky title. <br/> <br/>Sorry this didn''t do better for you, but I guess it landed about where you expected. And you got some good comments. <br/> <br/>Really, it''s not a pigeon? Well, then it''s some other intrusive bird poking its beak where it shouldn''t. There have been far greater shoehorns. <br/> <br/>Good geometry (of course) and really nice black and white conversion. I can safely say that in blind voting (and with that awesome title) this would have gotten a seven from me. Not that it would have put you in ribbon territory, but still...</td>', 'I''ve been out of touch the last week or so. I meant to follow up on your entry, as I didn''t get around to voting. Anyway, I sort of remember hastily suggesting this title -- probably in jest. But really, I love it! A quirky shot needs a quirky title.  Sorry this didn''t do better for you, but I guess it landed about where you expected. And you got some good comments.  Really, it''s not a pigeon? Well, then it''s some other intrusive bird poking its beak where it shouldn''t. There have been far greater shoehorns.  Good geometry (of course) and really nice black and white conversion. I can safely say that in blind voting (and with that awesome title) this would have gotten a seven from me. Not that it would have put you in ribbon territory, but still...', '2009-07-31 22:38:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(5592970, 808378, 83313, '<td valign="top">It''s sharp, clear, an interesting flock of birds. About the only possible flaw I can see is the waves are right behind the birds, so they don''t stand out as well as they good. Minor nitpick, really. Didn''t deserve to place this low, but It looks like you got slammed with DNMC votes. Turned out mine was not a pigeon either, but with only the tail feathers showing, I suppose few people realized it.<br/> <br/>I gave this a 7. Still fits the spirit of the theme, I think. Maybe we should do seagulls next time, then all the people who live inland can shoehorn pigeons into the challenge.</td>', 'It''s sharp, clear, an interesting flock of birds. About the only possible flaw I can see is the waves are right behind the birds, so they don''t stand out as well as they good. Minor nitpick, really. Didn''t deserve to place this low, but It looks like you got slammed with DNMC votes. Turned out mine was not a pigeon either, but with only the tail feathers showing, I suppose few people realized it. I gave this a 7. Still fits the spirit of the theme, I think. Maybe we should do seagulls next time, then all the people who live inland can shoehorn pigeons into the challenge.', '2009-07-31 22:46:08.000000', NULL, 0),
